1
00:00:00,142 --> 00:00:04,529
Sometimes the best place for a one-click
button is right in the middle of a reply.

2
00:00:04,609 --> 00:00:09,222
With Klick-Zen, your agents can drop one
into any ticket response, with just a

3
00:00:09,222 --> 00:00:09,577
click.

4
00:00:09,657 --> 00:00:14,189
Write your reply in the Zendesk ticket
editor as usual, and place your cursor

5
00:00:14,189 --> 00:00:15,778
where the button should go.

6
00:00:15,858 --> 00:00:19,354
Then click the Klick-Zen icon in the
editor toolbar.

7
00:00:19,434 --> 00:00:23,388
A pop-up shows the buttons in your
account, each one pictured just as it

8
00:00:23,388 --> 00:00:24,925
looks, so you pick by sight.

9
00:00:25,005 --> 00:00:29,754
Click one, and it lands right in your
message, exactly as your customer will see

10
00:00:29,754 --> 00:00:29,932
it.

11
00:00:30,012 --> 00:00:34,397
Want to give your customer a choice? Add a
second button right beside the first.

12
00:00:34,477 --> 00:00:39,199
Klick-Zen fills in this ticket's details
as each button goes in, so every link is

13
00:00:39,199 --> 00:00:39,899
ready to go.

14
00:00:39,979 --> 00:00:44,145
Add a closing line, send your reply, and
you're done.

15
00:00:44,225 --> 00:00:49,236
It's perfect for the moments an automation
won't catch: confirming a fix, gathering

16
00:00:49,236 --> 00:00:51,168
details, or offering next steps.

17
00:00:51,248 --> 00:00:56,191
Find Klick-Zen on the Zendesk Marketplace,
and put one-click answers into every

18
00:00:56,191 --> 00:00:56,566
reply.
